# Exemplars — the Range, Not the Shape

> **SETUP AGENT:** copy this file to `protocol/exemplars.md` as-is, keeping the
> PROVISIONAL marker. The seed below has no learner in it. The tutor replaces seed
> entries with the learner's own days as they happen (D14), keeping 4–5 that contrast;
> when the last seed entry is gone, delete the marker.

> **PROVISIONAL — seed entries.** These are *kinds* of day, not this learner's days.
> Replace each with a real one as soon as a real one exists.

A few days that worked. **They are here because they differ from each other.** Read them
as a spread: the brief is to land somewhere this set has not been yet, with what made each
of them work. Never copy one's order of beats, its opening or its length. A day shaped
like any of these has failed, however well it executes.

This file replaces reading past scripts as models (banned in `constitution.md` → Fresh
Execution). When an entry stops being true, replace it with a day that is, and keep the
set contrasting. Four or five, never more: a large set is a template library.

---

## 1. The ask — a page of questions, no story owed (seed)

**The kind of day:** a short page of untested words in the read form. The learner writes
meanings; the tutor grades the meaning, reveals, and records.
**Why this kind works:** no preamble. It is quick, honest (asking is not self-marking),
and it changes what every later lesson is made of — the tutor stops re-teaching what was
already known.
**The quality to carry:** the shortest route to the truth about a learner is a question. A
day can be small and still be the most useful of the month.

## 2. The teardown — a tape they failed, taken apart (seed)

**The kind of day:** an overheard tape the learner mostly missed. They caught who and
what, and "most of this I didn't catch" is reframed as the pass it is. Then it is taken
apart line by line, and the learner's own questions set the agenda.
**Why this kind works:** the material is a real failure, not a constructed exercise.
**The quality to carry:** structure explained on a sound already heard is dense learning;
the sound alone on repeat is not.

## 3. The commission — their question, paid off first (seed)

**The kind of day:** the learner asked about a pair of words that collide. The tutor pays
it off before any demand — and when the full explanation does not fix the collision under
load, changes method mid-lesson (hand one form over as a single chunk) and says why.
**Why this kind works:** the lesson follows their curiosity, and the plan bends to the
evidence inside the session.
**The quality to carry:** a plan is a first guess.

---

**What these share** is the whole lesson of this file: each is built on something true
about the learner — a real error, a real question, a real gap — never on a word list the
machine assumed they lacked.
